{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794245160,"nonce":"6jXSs0y/pjJ4pE+0bjGa5UZ6xs0=","title":"Periodic re-mesh fails when a side face is split into several surfaces","message":"_apply_periodic passes the main and secondary surface lists of a periodic face pair to gmsh setPeriodic in label order. gmsh pairs the lists by position, so as soon as a side face is split into several surfaces (a stack of layers, each its own region) the pieces are mismatched. The lists also include an inner body's own faces that carry the same auto-name (the side wall of a hole box is 'left'/'right' of that box). Those are interfaces, not the cell's sides, and they shift the translation read from the bounding boxes.\n\nError: 'No corresponding point ... for periodic connection of surface 6 to 1'.\n\nReproduction: a box cell of four or more z-layers plus an inner hole box, N1E field, ties u(left) - u(right) and u(front) - u(back). Test: tests/test_fem_nedelec_periodic.py::test_periodic_remesh_pairs_each_face_piece_with_its_own_partner.\n\nFix: keep only exterior surfaces (one adjacent volume), and pair each secondary piece with the main piece its translated bounding box lands on; raise if a piece has no partner.","files":null}]}